                                                "sense_id": "8108ec6e-611e-3385-a608-bcb2ff3cae23",
                                                "text": "Either way, a set of antioxidants worked to reduce the levels of ROS, and the [fruit] flies could live to the ripe old age of 40 days… if not a teensy bit longer! But most importantly, this demonstrated that the death from lack of sleep was not only correlated with the production of ROS, but caused by it."
